---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config';
import { href } from '../lib';
const updated = 'November 22, 2026';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy" description={`How ${SITE.title} collects, uses and protects information about visitors.`}>
  <article class="post prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="page-lead">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    <p>This Privacy Policy explains what information {SITE.title} ("we", "us", "this site") collects when you visit
      {' '}<a href={SITE.url}>{SITE.url.replace(/^https?:\/\//, '')}</a>, how it is used, and the choices you have.
      By using this site, you agree to the practices described here.</p>

    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <p>We do not ask you to create an account, and we do not sell personal information. The site itself does not
      collect your name or email unless you contact us directly. We do use third-party services that may collect
      information automatically, as described below.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Usage data.</strong> Pages visited, time on page, referring site, approximate location (country/city),
        browser, device type and similar technical data.</li>
      <li><strong>Information you send us.</strong> If you email us, we receive your email address and whatever you
        include in the message. We use it only to reply.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
    <p>Cookies are small text files stored on your device. This site and its partners use cookies and similar
      technologies to measure traffic, remember preferences and, in the future, show advertising.
      You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings; the site will still work.</p>

    <h2>Google Analytics</h2>
    <p>We use Google Analytics 4 to understand how visitors use the site, so we can improve our content.
      Google Analytics uses cookies to collect usage data, which is processed by Google.
      Learn more in <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">How Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.
      You can opt out with the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.</p>

    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>We may display ads served by Google AdSense and its partners. Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies
      to serve ads based on your previous visits to this and other websites. Google's use of advertising cookies enables
      it and its partners to serve ads to you based on your visits to this site and/or other sites on the internet.</p>
    <p>You may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a>.
      You can also opt out of some third-party vendors' use of cookies for personalized advertising at
      {' '}<a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener">www.aboutads.info</a>.
      Visitors in the European Economic Area, the UK and Switzerland will be asked for consent before personalized ads or
      non-essential cookies are used.</p>

    <h2>Embedded content</h2>
    <p>Articles may include embedded YouTube videos. We use YouTube's privacy-enhanced mode (youtube-nocookie.com),
      but YouTube may still collect data when you play a video. Fonts are loaded from Google Fonts, which receives your
      IP address in order to deliver them. If comments are enabled on a post, they are provided by GitHub through
      Giscus, and are subject to <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener">GitHub's Privacy Statement</a>.
      Embedded content behaves the same way as if you visited the other website directly.</p>

    <h2>How we use information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To operate, maintain and improve the site and its content.</li>
      <li>To understand which articles are useful to readers.</li>
      <li>To respond to messages you send us.</li>
      <li>To show advertising that helps keep the site free.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>Depending on where you live (for example under the GDPR in the EU/UK or the CCPA/CPRA in California), you may have
      the right to access, correct or delete personal information, or to object to or limit certain processing.
      Because we hold very little personal data ourselves, most requests are best handled through the tools linked above.
      For anything else, <a href={href('contact/')}>contact us</a>.</p>

    <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>This site is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from them.</p>

    <h2>Third-party links</h2>
    <p>We link to other websites, such as company investor relations pages. We are not responsible for their privacy practices.</p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy from time to time. Changes take effect when posted on this page, and the date above will be updated.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about this policy? Visit our <a href={href('contact/')}>Contact page</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
